<node id="11131198" title="Re^4: Useless use of string in return statement" created="2021-04-13 11:50:02" updated="2021-04-13 11:50:02" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;Not to mention that return $a ? $a : $b; can always* be written as return $a || $b;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nitpick: &lt;c&gt;$a&lt;/c&gt; and &lt;c&gt;$b&lt;/c&gt; should not be understood as stand-ins for "anything", since &lt;c&gt;@a || @b&lt;/c&gt; is &lt;i&gt;not&lt;/i&gt; the same as &lt;c&gt;@a ? @a : @b&lt;/c&gt;, since the former imposes scalar context on &lt;c&gt;@a&lt;/c&gt; (and not on &lt;c&gt;@b&lt;/c&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
